('Entrepreneurship, Business & Fundraising','ECON 252: Financial Markets — Yale University','Robert Shiller''s Yale course on how financial institutions manage risk and foster enterprise: securities, insurance, banking, behavioral finance, and financial crises, delivered via Open Yale Courses, Coursera, and YouTube with full lectures, transcripts, syllabus, readings, and exams.'),
('Entrepreneurship, Business & Fundraising','Entrepreneurship (textbook) — Rice University (OpenStax)','OpenStax''s peer-reviewed introductory entrepreneurship textbook (15 chapters): the entrepreneurial mindset, opportunity recognition, business models, financing, marketing, and innovation, with review and case questions throughout.'),
('Entrepreneurship, Business & Fundraising','Entrepreneurship Specialization (Wharton) — University of Pennsylvania','Wharton School''s Coursera specialization on the conception, design, organization, and management of new enterprises: developing the opportunity, launching, growth strategies, financing and profitability, plus a capstone project.'),
('Mathematics for Computer Science','6.042J Mathematics for Computer Science — Massachusetts Institute of Technology','MIT''s discrete mathematics course for computer scientists (Leighton and van Dijk): proofs, logic, induction, graph theory, number theory, and probability, with lecture videos, problem sets, and exams with solutions.'),
('Mathematics for Computer Science','18.06 Linear Algebra — Massachusetts Institute of Technology','Gilbert Strang''s celebrated linear algebra course — matrices, vector spaces, eigenvalues, and least squares, the mathematical backbone of machine learning — with full lecture videos, problem sets with solutions, and exams with solutions.'),
('Mathematics for Computer Science','18.01 Single Variable Calculus — Massachusetts Institute of Technology','MIT''s first-semester calculus course: differentiation and integration of functions of one variable, the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, and applications, with lecture notes, problem sets with solutions, and exams with solutions (an OCW Scholar version adds segmented lecture videos for independent study).')
